1
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:46,067
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:01:00,999 --> 00:01:01,833
‎Get off me!

3
00:01:02,709 --> 00:01:05,170
‎-Mr. Ma! Keep still!
‎-Get off me!

4
00:01:05,253 --> 00:01:06,963
‎Go away!

5
00:01:07,672 --> 00:01:08,756
‎You said you weren't afraid!

6
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,427
‎No! No!

7
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:13,595
‎Go away!

8
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:17,557
‎He's off your back now!

9
00:01:18,141 --> 00:01:20,268
‎He's gone!

10
00:01:20,894 --> 00:01:22,353
‎He's gone!

11
00:01:22,854 --> 00:01:23,688
‎He's gone?

12
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:25,231
‎He's gone?

13
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:36,284
‎Do you see the kid?

14
00:01:39,412 --> 00:01:41,623
‎Yes. I see him.

15
00:01:48,755 --> 00:01:50,590
‎EPISODE 4

16
00:02:10,068 --> 00:02:10,944
‎What…

17
00:02:56,030 --> 00:02:57,281
‎I'll call it in.

18
00:02:57,365 --> 00:02:58,199
‎Okay.

19
00:03:05,456 --> 00:03:07,417
‎Hey, are you all right?

20
00:03:08,209 --> 00:03:10,211
‎The back… In the back.

21
00:03:10,294 --> 00:03:11,671
‎-The back.
‎-In the back?

22
00:03:12,255 --> 00:03:13,840
‎-Look in the back.
‎-Hold on.

23
00:03:27,311 --> 00:03:29,772
‎My boy. He's okay, isn't he?

24
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:33,901
‎He's…

25
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:36,279
‎He's okay, isn't he?

26
00:03:46,289 --> 00:03:47,415
‎He's warm.

27
00:03:50,376 --> 00:03:51,377
‎Good.

28
00:03:53,338 --> 00:03:54,339
‎That's good.

29
00:04:11,856 --> 00:04:14,650
‎EMERGENCY SERVICES

30
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,119
‎Gang-uk.

31
00:04:47,892 --> 00:04:50,436
‎Oh, no. Hold on.

32
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:52,814
‎-There's someone here!
‎-Help!

33
00:04:52,897 --> 00:04:54,399
‎-In here.
‎-Over here!

34
00:04:54,482 --> 00:04:56,776
‎There's someone here! Over here!

35
00:04:57,318 --> 00:04:58,861
‎-Where are they?
‎-In there.

36
00:05:00,154 --> 00:05:01,656
‎The child is alive!

37
00:05:01,739 --> 00:05:04,033
‎Her breathing is shallow. Get the oxygen!

38
00:05:04,117 --> 00:05:08,037
‎Ju-young, Daddy will make lots of money
‎and buy you plenty of toys.

39
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:09,789
‎Be good and listen to Grandma, okay?

40
00:05:09,872 --> 00:05:11,124
‎-Okay.
‎-Good.

41
00:05:12,041 --> 00:05:15,128
‎-Do you like that toy that much, Da-young?
‎-Yes.

42
00:05:16,879 --> 00:05:18,172
‎Ju-young.

43
00:05:18,256 --> 00:05:20,716
‎You're the big brother,
‎so look after your sister.

44
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:46,409
‎We found an injured little girl.

45
00:05:47,076 --> 00:05:48,744
‎Yes. We're loading her up.

46
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:52,748
‎-Get that for me.
‎-Careful.

47
00:05:58,087 --> 00:05:59,046
‎All done.

48
00:05:59,881 --> 00:06:01,007
‎Let's go.

49
00:07:13,996 --> 00:07:16,707
‎When did all this start?

50
00:07:25,341 --> 00:07:26,425
‎I was in a yacht accident

51
00:07:27,927 --> 00:07:29,887
‎when I was in university.

52
00:07:31,931 --> 00:07:32,932
‎Yeo-ri!

53
00:07:35,476 --> 00:07:38,354
‎I stopped breathing completely.

54
00:07:43,776 --> 00:07:45,611
‎Then miraculously, I came to.

55
00:07:53,995 --> 00:07:56,205
‎But my friend who fell in with me…

56
00:07:57,957 --> 00:07:59,083
‎didn't make it.

57
00:08:00,376 --> 00:08:02,086
‎We have two different words

58
00:08:02,169 --> 00:08:04,130
‎that mean "grave," depending on the shape.

59
00:08:04,213 --> 00:08:08,092
‎Some have a high, rounded top,
‎which we call "bun."

60
00:08:08,175 --> 00:08:11,929
‎If the body is buried underground
‎with a flat top, it's called "myo."

61
00:08:12,847 --> 00:08:16,892
‎There are three different kinds
‎of high, rounded grave tops.

62
00:08:16,976 --> 00:08:19,061
‎The most common type is…

63
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:20,938
‎After that,

64
00:08:22,106 --> 00:08:25,359
‎-I kept seeing Ji-hwan, who had died.
‎-Ji-hwan.

65
00:08:29,238 --> 00:08:30,573
‎What's the matter?

66
00:08:34,118 --> 00:08:35,536
‎That's when it began.

67
00:08:37,705 --> 00:08:39,457
‎-It's a lovely day.
‎-It is.

68
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:41,000
‎The weather is amazing.

69
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:43,669
‎-Did you have something to eat?
‎-No, not yet.

70
00:08:44,962 --> 00:08:48,549
‎Ghosts that others couldn't see
‎appeared in front of me.

71
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:49,884
‎Are you all right?

72
00:08:52,261 --> 00:08:55,181
‎-And anyone whose hands touched mine
‎-Thank you.

73
00:08:56,641 --> 00:08:58,726
‎started seeing them.

74
00:09:02,188 --> 00:09:03,022
‎What's that?

75
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:12,323
‎-She sees ghosts.
‎-She can see stuff.

76
00:09:12,406 --> 00:09:14,492
‎"If you so much as touch Cheon Yeo-ri,

77
00:09:14,992 --> 00:09:16,869
‎ghosts will latch onto you too."

78
00:09:17,536 --> 00:09:20,623
‎"If you stick around her,
‎you'll ‎be ‎cursed ‎too."

79
00:09:21,749 --> 00:09:23,626
‎Rumors like that started to spread.

80
00:09:25,586 --> 00:09:26,754
‎Ever since then,

81
00:09:27,421 --> 00:09:31,300
‎I've been living alone,
‎like a living ghost.

82
00:09:36,222 --> 00:09:38,974
‎I tried to live a decent life though.

83
00:09:39,809 --> 00:09:41,686
‎There's a lot you can do on your own.

84
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:44,355
‎Once you get used to it,

85
00:09:46,232 --> 00:09:47,483
‎being alone isn't so bad.

86
00:09:50,861 --> 00:09:54,323
‎I suspected you as an accomplice,
‎not knowing about your background.

87
00:09:57,201 --> 00:09:58,244
‎I'm sorry.

88
00:10:00,329 --> 00:10:02,415
‎I got you all wrong too,
‎when we first met.

89
00:10:04,125 --> 00:10:05,501
‎What do we do now?

90
00:10:06,001 --> 00:10:07,670
‎More ghosts will come for you.

91
00:10:09,338 --> 00:10:10,548
‎It can't be helped.

92
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,928
‎What happened to the other people
‎you came in contact with?

93
00:10:18,097 --> 00:10:19,557
‎From what I know,

94
00:10:20,474 --> 00:10:23,686
‎I think they saw ghosts for about a month.

95
00:10:24,937 --> 00:10:25,813
‎And after that?

96
00:10:26,355 --> 00:10:27,857
‎After a month,

97
00:10:28,441 --> 00:10:30,818
‎the ghosts will stop coming for you,

98
00:10:30,901 --> 00:10:32,903
‎as long as you stay away from me.

99
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:39,201
‎I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.

100
00:10:40,536 --> 00:10:43,372
‎Let's stay away from each other
‎as best we can.

101
00:10:44,248 --> 00:10:45,291
‎If you're around me,

102
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:47,793
‎you might become miserable.

103
00:10:48,627 --> 00:10:49,837
‎Why would you say that?

104
00:10:50,796 --> 00:10:51,714
‎Bye then.

105
00:10:53,966 --> 00:10:54,800
‎Wait.

106
00:11:04,685 --> 00:11:07,938
‎This is day one.
‎The start of that one month.

107
00:11:08,606 --> 00:11:09,690
‎But still…

108
00:11:09,774 --> 00:11:10,900
‎I finally understand

109
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:13,110
‎what you meant

110
00:11:14,195 --> 00:11:15,654
‎in Jeju Island.

111
00:11:16,197 --> 00:11:17,323
‎Thank you.

112
00:11:18,782 --> 00:11:20,618
‎I might be used to how things are,

113
00:11:21,619 --> 00:11:23,704
‎but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.

114
00:11:27,166 --> 00:11:28,918
‎It must've been so hard to live with.

115
00:12:03,202 --> 00:12:04,245
‎I'm exhausted.

116
00:12:04,995 --> 00:12:06,872
‎Let me rest tonight.

117
00:12:06,956 --> 00:12:08,207
‎I have a lot on my mind.

118
00:12:25,599 --> 00:12:27,142
‎Will he be okay?

119
00:12:30,271 --> 00:12:31,772
‎It'll be really hard at first.

120
00:13:36,086 --> 00:13:36,920
‎Why…

121
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,802
‎-What was that about?
‎-I don't know.

122
00:13:45,929 --> 00:13:46,930
‎What's so funny?

123
00:13:50,184 --> 00:13:51,101
‎Your name.

124
00:14:05,908 --> 00:14:08,452
‎Oh, my heart hurts…

125
00:14:54,289 --> 00:14:55,916
‎CEO CHEON YEO-RI

126
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,459
‎I wasn't aware of this,

127
00:14:58,210 --> 00:14:59,545
‎but apparently this is a thing.

128
00:14:59,628 --> 00:15:01,338
‎PVC STICKER FOR CARS

129
00:15:01,422 --> 00:15:03,424
‎Print some and put them in the kids' zone.

130
00:15:03,507 --> 00:15:04,967
‎Yes, ma'am.

131
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:08,345
‎One more thing.

132
00:15:09,471 --> 00:15:11,682
‎How old is your child now, Ms. Eom?

133
00:15:11,765 --> 00:15:13,892
‎-Four years old.
‎-I see.

134
00:15:15,436 --> 00:15:16,478
‎In that case…

135
00:15:24,236 --> 00:15:26,363
‎If your child happens to like

136
00:15:27,239 --> 00:15:28,866
‎toys or dolls…

137
00:15:34,538 --> 00:15:35,539
‎Thank you.

138
00:16:00,105 --> 00:16:01,356
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk?

139
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:02,775
‎Yes.

140
00:16:02,858 --> 00:16:06,361
‎I think they've been in touch
‎ever since he came here to see her.

141
00:16:08,030 --> 00:16:10,949
‎Are you saying they're dating?

142
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:12,659
‎I can't say for sure.

143
00:16:14,161 --> 00:16:15,162
‎Okay.

144
00:16:27,966 --> 00:16:29,760
‎What's all this?

145
00:16:30,344 --> 00:16:31,345
‎Mr. Ma.

146
00:16:32,096 --> 00:16:33,388
‎I thought you had no religion.

147
00:16:33,472 --> 00:16:34,723
‎I converted to polytheism.

148
00:16:34,807 --> 00:16:36,391
‎-Polytheism?
‎-Yeah.

149
00:16:36,475 --> 00:16:38,519
‎Are you trying to integrate all religions?

150
00:16:39,686 --> 00:16:40,938
‎You believe in all this?

151
00:16:41,021 --> 00:16:44,066
‎Who knows which one actually counts?

152
00:16:44,942 --> 00:16:48,445
‎There's bound to be one
‎that'll scare them.

153
00:16:48,529 --> 00:16:51,573
‎Who exactly are you trying to scare?

154
00:16:52,199 --> 00:16:55,911
‎Well, the punks I deal with
‎are a dangerous bunch.

155
00:16:55,994 --> 00:16:59,665
‎You never know when
‎and which deity will come through.

156
00:16:59,748 --> 00:17:02,626
‎You do look like you could use some faith.

157
00:17:03,627 --> 00:17:06,588
‎Why don't you come over this weekend?
‎I'll keep you entertained.

158
00:17:06,672 --> 00:17:08,382
‎Oh, my mom's calling.

159
00:17:08,465 --> 00:17:10,884
‎-Hello? Hi, Mom.
‎-You know,

160
00:17:10,968 --> 00:17:12,886
‎that's a completely ridiculous idea.

161
00:17:13,512 --> 00:17:14,513
‎It's the weekend.

162
00:17:14,596 --> 00:17:17,766
‎If I were to suddenly go crazy,
‎then maybe I'd visit.

163
00:17:18,892 --> 00:17:19,810
‎You're right.

164
00:17:19,893 --> 00:17:21,603
‎Weekends are precious.

165
00:17:21,687 --> 00:17:24,481
‎Night duty is better than going home.
‎I'll see you in the office.

166
00:17:24,565 --> 00:17:26,984
‎I do wonder what you do on weekends.

167
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:28,402
‎What should we do?

168
00:17:29,027 --> 00:17:31,196
‎Do you play video games? Or board games?

169
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:32,406
‎Not board games.

170
00:17:32,489 --> 00:17:35,367
‎Let's watch a movie.
‎Something really steamy.

171
00:17:36,034 --> 00:17:37,703
‎-I can't wait.
‎-Good.

172
00:17:37,786 --> 00:17:38,745
‎I'm excited.

173
00:17:42,916 --> 00:17:43,959
‎I can't wait.

174
00:17:49,882 --> 00:17:51,842
‎Don't laugh.

175
00:17:51,925 --> 00:17:53,594
‎You call this steamy?

176
00:17:53,677 --> 00:17:55,470
‎It's a darn old movie too.

177
00:17:55,554 --> 00:17:57,431
‎You called me over just to watch this?

178
00:17:57,514 --> 00:18:00,392
‎Come on, I need to build up some courage.

179
00:18:01,268 --> 00:18:02,895
‎Help me out with some moral support.

180
00:18:04,730 --> 00:18:05,772
‎Pil-dong.

181
00:18:07,232 --> 00:18:09,109
‎Why do ghosts appear
‎in girls' high schools?

182
00:18:09,818 --> 00:18:11,737
‎Well, I mean…

183
00:18:13,197 --> 00:18:16,950
‎wouldn't it be ridiculous
‎if they were to haunt boys' schools?

184
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:23,498
‎Pil-dong, why do ghosts
‎always cling to people's backs?

185
00:18:23,582 --> 00:18:24,625
‎Well…

186
00:18:25,584 --> 00:18:29,922
‎If they were to cling to people
‎from the front like this,

187
00:18:30,005 --> 00:18:32,591
‎wouldn't that look ridiculous?

188
00:18:34,509 --> 00:18:37,888
‎Pil-dong, why do ghosts
‎have straight hair?

189
00:18:38,639 --> 00:18:40,515
‎Do you think ghosts

190
00:18:41,642 --> 00:18:44,853
‎would get perms
‎to keep the curls bouncy?

191
00:18:44,937 --> 00:18:46,271
‎Wouldn't that look ridiculous?

192
00:18:47,314 --> 00:18:48,273
‎You're right.

193
00:18:48,357 --> 00:18:52,194
‎Could you just think
‎before you ask a question?

194
00:18:56,823 --> 00:18:58,408
‎-Pil-dong.
‎-What?

195
00:18:58,492 --> 00:19:00,786
‎What is it now?
‎You wanted to watch a movie.

196
00:19:00,869 --> 00:19:02,496
‎It's a sunny Saturday afternoon,

197
00:19:02,579 --> 00:19:04,790
‎and the two of us guys
‎are watching a goddamn movie.

198
00:19:04,873 --> 00:19:06,124
‎-I'm leaving.
‎-What?

199
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:08,126
‎You threatened me
‎with night duty to come here,

200
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:11,797
‎-but I can't stand being with you.
‎-Pil-dong, it's not like that.

201
00:19:12,422 --> 00:19:14,383
‎He thinks I'm his lackey

202
00:19:14,466 --> 00:19:16,468
‎-since I'm at his beck and call.
‎-Pil-dong.

203
00:19:16,551 --> 00:19:18,762
‎-Wait, I'll buy you tuna sashimi.
‎-I'm not some lackey.

204
00:19:18,845 --> 00:19:19,888
‎I'll order it right now.

205
00:19:22,266 --> 00:19:25,394
‎-I want some belly meat.
‎-Of course.

206
00:19:25,477 --> 00:19:27,729
‎-I only eat Pacific bluefin.
‎-Right, of course.

207
00:19:29,106 --> 00:19:30,148
‎Pacific bluefin.

208
00:19:31,525 --> 00:19:32,359
‎Belly.

209
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,072
‎Pil-dong, wait for me!

210
00:19:47,249 --> 00:19:48,917
‎It's only been a week.

211
00:19:51,878 --> 00:19:53,463
‎It's almost time.

212
00:19:53,547 --> 00:19:54,381
‎Right.

213
00:19:54,464 --> 00:19:55,549
‎Let's go.

214
00:20:22,326 --> 00:20:24,411
‎PROSECUTOR MA

215
00:20:30,625 --> 00:20:33,086
‎Yeo-ri, please, please pick up.

216
00:20:33,712 --> 00:20:34,546
‎Sorry.

217
00:20:35,172 --> 00:20:36,340
‎It's best that you and I

218
00:20:37,090 --> 00:20:39,134
‎don't cross paths,
‎not even over the phone.

219
00:20:41,303 --> 00:20:44,264
‎The call cannot be connected.
‎You will be redirected to voicemail…

220
00:22:11,393 --> 00:22:13,311
‎Ms. Cheon! Yeo-ri!

221
00:22:13,979 --> 00:22:15,730
‎Ms. Cheon! Yeo-ri!

222
00:22:21,153 --> 00:22:21,987
‎What the heck?

223
00:22:23,947 --> 00:22:24,823
‎Who is it?

224
00:22:26,575 --> 00:22:28,618
‎-I'll leave your package out here.
‎-Okay.

225
00:22:32,956 --> 00:22:33,832
‎It's just the delivery man.

226
00:22:43,508 --> 00:22:44,342
‎Yeo-ri.

227
00:22:46,845 --> 00:22:48,972
‎Wait, why is it closing?

228
00:22:51,516 --> 00:22:53,643
‎If someone calls, at least pick up.

229
00:22:53,727 --> 00:22:56,062
‎I have so many things to ask you.

230
00:22:58,607 --> 00:22:59,524
‎Ms. Cheon.

231
00:23:02,319 --> 00:23:03,695
‎Yeo-ri.

232
00:23:03,778 --> 00:23:05,071
‎I'm sorry.

233
00:23:06,114 --> 00:23:08,074
‎I think this is for the best.

234
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:11,661
‎I came all the way here.
‎Can't we talk inside?

235
00:23:15,707 --> 00:23:16,958
‎It's tough, isn't it?

236
00:23:34,392 --> 00:23:36,228
‎I could barely get through a week.

237
00:23:38,563 --> 00:23:41,149
‎How did you manage to endure it
‎for ten whole years?

238
00:23:45,237 --> 00:23:46,488
‎To tell you the truth,

239
00:23:47,072 --> 00:23:49,407
‎I blamed you at first, and I was furious.

240
00:23:50,075 --> 00:23:51,826
‎So I came here to complain.

241
00:23:53,370 --> 00:23:55,080
‎But seeing you here,

242
00:23:56,414 --> 00:23:59,084
‎I realize how cowardly and pathetic I am.

243
00:24:02,045 --> 00:24:03,213
‎Unlike you,

244
00:24:04,422 --> 00:24:06,258
‎I just have to hold out for a month.

245
00:24:09,010 --> 00:24:11,846
‎Compared to you,
‎my suffering is a drop in the ocean.

246
00:24:17,644 --> 00:24:20,021
‎Sorry for coming all this way
‎and making a fuss.

247
00:24:22,023 --> 00:24:23,024
‎Don't be.

248
00:24:24,609 --> 00:24:26,695
‎I feel bad for you just the same.

249
00:24:27,445 --> 00:24:29,739
‎Don't be.
‎I'll try to get through it on my own.

250
00:24:31,658 --> 00:24:32,701
‎I'm an adult, after all.

251
00:24:34,244 --> 00:24:35,745
‎Much more so than you were back then.

252
00:24:42,294 --> 00:24:43,295
‎Bye then.

253
00:24:49,467 --> 00:24:50,302
‎Wait.

254
00:24:55,724 --> 00:24:56,558
‎How about…

255
00:24:59,936 --> 00:25:01,271
‎we try this?

256
00:25:12,157 --> 00:25:14,367
‎I don't know if it'll help,

257
00:25:15,201 --> 00:25:18,288
‎but I have a few tips of my ‎own.

258
00:25:19,622 --> 00:25:22,459
‎The ghosts that visit you early on

259
00:25:22,542 --> 00:25:26,212
‎will be the nasty ones
‎that harass and torment others.

260
00:25:28,214 --> 00:25:29,716
‎But don't let it show.

261
00:25:30,759 --> 00:25:34,387
‎Their favorite moment ‎is
‎when ‎you ‎wake ‎up from sleep paralysis.

262
00:25:34,971 --> 00:25:37,599
‎Do your best to hide that you're scared

263
00:25:37,682 --> 00:25:40,185
‎and try to sleep as if you don't care.

264
00:25:41,853 --> 00:25:44,397
‎Make them see that you're not affected.

265
00:25:46,858 --> 00:25:48,860
‎Why? Is it not working tonight?

266
00:25:48,943 --> 00:25:51,905
‎That's strange.
‎He's not usually like this.

267
00:25:52,614 --> 00:25:55,784
‎I'm sure he saw us though.

268
00:26:07,504 --> 00:26:08,838
‎Have you spoken to them?

269
00:26:11,424 --> 00:26:12,258
‎Good.

270
00:26:12,842 --> 00:26:15,178
‎Avoid talking to them at all costs.

271
00:26:15,845 --> 00:26:19,682
‎Ignore them ‎and ‎hang ‎in ‎there
‎for as long as you can.

272
00:26:25,897 --> 00:26:26,940
‎Good job.

273
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:56,761
‎What's wrong?

274
00:26:59,973 --> 00:27:01,391
‎You must be at a crosswalk.

275
00:27:01,474 --> 00:27:03,685
‎What do I do? He's staring at me.

276
00:27:03,768 --> 00:27:05,979
‎Step on the gas as if you don't see him.

277
00:27:06,062 --> 00:27:06,980
‎What?

278
00:27:07,647 --> 00:27:09,274
‎-Do it.
‎-But…

279
00:27:24,914 --> 00:27:27,250
‎The more you know,
‎the more you can handle.

280
00:27:46,436 --> 00:27:47,270
‎I lose.

281
00:27:53,902 --> 00:27:56,029
‎PROSECUTOR MA GANG-UK

282
00:27:56,112 --> 00:27:58,698
‎I'm almost there. It's nearly over.

283
00:28:06,122 --> 00:28:08,666
‎I just have to last one more week.

284
00:28:08,750 --> 00:28:11,377
‎-Oh, right.
‎-What? What is it now?

285
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:13,630
‎I got distracted and forgot the basics.

286
00:28:15,381 --> 00:28:16,216
‎Sprinkling salt.

287
00:28:22,430 --> 00:28:24,224
‎Hurl it down hard, with force.

288
00:28:38,112 --> 00:28:39,072
‎Garlic.

289
00:28:40,907 --> 00:28:42,867
‎-Hey, Ma.
‎-No, thanks.

290
00:28:42,951 --> 00:28:44,869
‎-Hi.
‎-Sit with us.

291
00:28:44,953 --> 00:28:46,246
‎I have to go through something.

292
00:28:46,329 --> 00:28:47,872
‎-Enjoy yourselves.
‎-What?

293
00:28:47,956 --> 00:28:52,293
‎I hear they dislike food
‎with strong odors or flavors.

294
00:28:53,586 --> 00:28:56,297
‎In that sense, garlic is very effective.

295
00:29:03,763 --> 00:29:05,682
‎He's definitely acting a bit off.

296
00:29:06,516 --> 00:29:07,559
‎He's lost it.

297
00:29:07,642 --> 00:29:10,687
‎He keeps asking me things like,
‎"Why do ghosts always

298
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:13,064
‎have long, straight hair?"

299
00:29:14,065 --> 00:29:15,942
‎"Why do they cling to one's back?"

300
00:29:16,860 --> 00:29:19,529
‎There must be something about ghosts.

301
00:29:22,198 --> 00:29:23,700
‎Could he be possessed?

302
00:29:25,952 --> 00:29:26,911
‎Look.

303
00:29:26,995 --> 00:29:28,538
‎Look at him stuffing his face
‎with all that garlic.

304
00:29:28,621 --> 00:29:30,540
‎-What's going on?
‎-What's gotten into him?

305
00:29:34,002 --> 00:29:36,004
‎You know, in movies,

306
00:29:36,087 --> 00:29:39,090
‎people who are possessed
‎stuff garlic down, then spit it out.

307
00:29:41,801 --> 00:29:44,345
‎That's Dracula. Vampires do that.

308
00:29:44,429 --> 00:29:46,639
‎-Oh, right.
‎-Korean ghosts hate glutinous rice

309
00:29:46,723 --> 00:29:47,891
‎-and red beans.
‎-Right.

310
00:29:49,642 --> 00:29:52,395
‎-It's the prosecutor general.
‎-I'm disturbing you all.

311
00:29:52,478 --> 00:29:54,063
‎It's fine. Stay seated.

312
00:29:54,147 --> 00:29:55,481
‎Let's eat over there.

313
00:30:08,620 --> 00:30:10,622
‎Which division are you in?

314
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:12,373
‎Yes, sir. I'm…

315
00:30:14,959 --> 00:30:17,879
‎I'm in the Cold Case Unit.
‎My name is Ma Gang-uk, sir.

316
00:30:17,962 --> 00:30:21,382
‎Oh, the team they decided to revamp?

317
00:30:22,133 --> 00:30:23,051
‎Yes.

318
00:30:24,886 --> 00:30:26,721
‎-So, sir.
‎-Mr. Ma.

319
00:30:26,804 --> 00:30:30,642
‎I appreciate the intention
‎behind revamping the Cold Case Unit.

320
00:30:33,061 --> 00:30:34,395
‎But the recent personnel transfer

321
00:30:35,688 --> 00:30:37,065
‎was influenced by an outside…

322
00:30:48,201 --> 00:30:50,411
‎-I'm so sorry.
‎-Clean him up.

323
00:30:50,495 --> 00:30:51,496
‎I'm sorry, sir.

324
00:30:51,579 --> 00:30:53,748
‎-Sir, let me…
‎-Oh, dear.

325
00:30:54,916 --> 00:30:56,334
‎I'm so sorry, sir. I was…

326
00:31:01,297 --> 00:31:02,757
‎He definitely did spit it out.

327
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:03,883
‎Oh, gosh.

328
00:31:10,932 --> 00:31:12,058
‎Yeo-ri.

329
00:31:12,141 --> 00:31:14,769
‎Show me your glass and champagne too.

330
00:31:14,852 --> 00:31:15,979
‎What do you mean?

331
00:31:16,062 --> 00:31:17,814
‎It'll be all over by tomorrow night.

332
00:31:17,897 --> 00:31:21,192
‎Let's celebrate with champagne,
‎even if it's over a video call.

333
00:31:24,362 --> 00:31:25,321
‎Give me a moment.

334
00:31:35,206 --> 00:31:37,875
‎It's like we're drinking alone,
‎but not quite.

335
00:31:37,959 --> 00:31:41,629
‎They say you shouldn't
‎pop the champagne too early though.

336
00:31:41,713 --> 00:31:43,006
‎It'll be fine.

337
00:31:43,089 --> 00:31:45,258
‎What could happen in just one day?

338
00:31:46,718 --> 00:31:48,678
‎As long as there aren't too many of them,

339
00:31:48,761 --> 00:31:51,014
‎I'm sure I can manage on my own for a day.

340
00:31:58,521 --> 00:31:59,522
‎Shall we?

341
00:32:03,317 --> 00:32:05,028
‎-Cheers.
‎-Cheers.

342
00:32:17,290 --> 00:32:18,291
‎Yeo-ri.

343
00:32:19,709 --> 00:32:21,419
‎Thank you for everything.

344
00:32:22,045 --> 00:32:24,047
‎I'm glad if I helped beat the fear.

345
00:32:24,130 --> 00:32:26,924
‎You didn't. I was scared the whole time.

346
00:32:27,008 --> 00:32:28,259
‎What?

347
00:32:29,052 --> 00:32:30,386
‎I was scared the whole time.

348
00:32:31,679 --> 00:32:33,765
‎They have no physical form,

349
00:32:33,848 --> 00:32:37,268
‎and they're not human,
‎so how could I not be scared?

350
00:32:38,478 --> 00:32:39,395
‎That's true.

351
00:32:40,521 --> 00:32:41,397
‎The truth is,

352
00:32:42,774 --> 00:32:45,234
‎I feel the same,
‎though I pretend not to be.

353
00:32:45,318 --> 00:32:46,152
‎Right?

354
00:32:46,736 --> 00:32:48,988
‎So I wasn't the only one to be scared.

355
00:32:49,489 --> 00:32:52,617
‎As soon as one ghost leaves,
‎another one appears.

356
00:32:52,700 --> 00:32:55,203
‎And why are there so many different kinds?

357
00:32:56,913 --> 00:32:58,664
‎I was terrified every single time.

358
00:33:00,708 --> 00:33:01,834
‎But I felt reassured…

359
00:33:04,045 --> 00:33:06,339
‎by your voice
‎that helped me through each time.

360
00:33:11,052 --> 00:33:13,262
‎That's how I was able to get through it.

361
00:33:20,311 --> 00:33:22,605
‎I guess that means I protected you, right?

362
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:24,899
‎That's pretty rewarding.

363
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:27,610
‎Thank you, Yeo-ri.

364
00:33:29,987 --> 00:33:32,824
‎Oh, and I did some thinking.

365
00:33:33,574 --> 00:33:36,452
‎Wouldn't it be okay
‎to interact virtually like this?

366
00:33:37,453 --> 00:33:41,249
‎We can check on each other sometimes,
‎or ask for help if we need it.

367
00:33:42,208 --> 00:33:45,628
‎People make friends
‎through social media these days,

368
00:33:45,711 --> 00:33:47,588
‎and even travel online
‎without being there.

369
00:33:52,760 --> 00:33:53,636
‎No.

370
00:33:54,804 --> 00:33:56,472
‎It's best if we don't do that.

371
00:34:02,979 --> 00:34:05,481
‎If you just get through one more day,

372
00:34:06,315 --> 00:34:09,026
‎we can both return
‎to our everyday lives, right?

373
00:34:10,570 --> 00:34:12,071
‎Take care of yourself.

374
00:34:12,655 --> 00:34:14,157
‎Even if we meet by chance,

375
00:34:16,033 --> 00:34:16,909
‎let's pretend…

376
00:34:18,411 --> 00:34:19,579
‎to be strangers.

377
00:34:21,956 --> 00:34:22,999
‎Yeo-ri…

378
00:34:24,250 --> 00:34:25,418
‎Bye.

379
00:34:27,044 --> 00:34:27,920
‎CEO CHEON YEO-RI
‎CALL ENDED

380
00:35:11,672 --> 00:35:13,466
‎Wasn't that a bit too harsh?

381
00:35:14,217 --> 00:35:18,012
‎We'll pretend to be strangers
‎even if we meet by chance?

382
00:35:33,861 --> 00:35:35,238
‎Thank you for everything.

383
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:38,282
‎I was terrified every single time.

384
00:35:38,950 --> 00:35:40,243
‎But I felt reassured

385
00:35:40,826 --> 00:35:43,037
‎by your voice
‎that helped me through each time.

386
00:35:44,830 --> 00:35:46,874
‎That's how I was able to get through it.

387
00:35:56,968 --> 00:36:00,054
‎You said you could manage
‎on your own for a day.

388
00:36:00,137 --> 00:36:02,014
‎What ghost is it this time?

389
00:36:04,850 --> 00:36:05,935
‎CHEON HA-RI

390
00:36:08,938 --> 00:36:10,564
‎Why do you care who I'm talking to?

391
00:36:11,816 --> 00:36:12,817
‎And don't even think of

392
00:36:13,985 --> 00:36:15,903
‎bringing me down with that again.

393
00:36:23,035 --> 00:36:24,662
‎"What ghost is it this time?"

394
00:36:26,497 --> 00:36:28,791
‎She's definitely hiding something.

395
00:36:36,048 --> 00:36:37,925
‎-Min-hwan.
‎-Ha-ri.

396
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:40,886
‎I'm so touched.

397
00:36:40,970 --> 00:36:43,306
‎You offered to treat me,
‎and you actually came.

398
00:36:43,389 --> 00:36:44,223
‎What?

399
00:36:45,516 --> 00:36:48,311
‎Oh, sure. Is there anything you'd like?

400
00:36:48,394 --> 00:36:50,104
‎Whatever you like is fine.

401
00:36:50,187 --> 00:36:51,981
‎You're a gourmand.

402
00:36:54,442 --> 00:36:56,610
‎By the way, is something up with Yeo-ri?

403
00:36:57,570 --> 00:36:58,404
‎What?

404
00:36:58,487 --> 00:37:01,115
‎I called her a few times since I came,
‎but she didn't pick up.

405
00:37:04,243 --> 00:37:06,620
‎If she doesn't pick up,
‎she's putting up a wall.

406
00:37:07,246 --> 00:37:09,165
‎From what my mom told me,

407
00:37:09,248 --> 00:37:12,293
‎she seems to be seeing
‎some prosecutor pretty often.

408
00:37:12,793 --> 00:37:13,794
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk?

409
00:37:14,378 --> 00:37:15,421
‎How do you know his name?

410
00:37:17,506 --> 00:37:18,341
‎Ha-ri.

411
00:37:18,424 --> 00:37:20,176
‎If you care about someone,

412
00:37:20,259 --> 00:37:21,594
‎you naturally learn all about them.

413
00:37:42,531 --> 00:37:43,407
‎PRO GOLFER PARK'S EX JANG FOUND DEAD

414
00:37:43,491 --> 00:37:48,621
‎PARK WANTED AS LIKELY SUSPECT

415
00:37:48,704 --> 00:37:49,705
‎Damn it!

416
00:37:50,373 --> 00:37:52,958
‎So Cheon Yeo-ri reported it,
‎and that's how Ma found out?

417
00:37:53,042 --> 00:37:53,876
‎I'm sure of it.

418
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:58,964
‎No wonder they both went on
‎about my monumental fall.

419
00:38:00,132 --> 00:38:01,175
‎Seung-jae.

420
00:38:01,675 --> 00:38:03,010
‎What you said before.

421
00:38:03,594 --> 00:38:05,805
‎-Did you mean that?
‎-About what?

422
00:38:05,888 --> 00:38:07,473
‎You swore on your life

423
00:38:07,556 --> 00:38:10,643
‎that you'd help me take over Reina
‎once you get out of here.

424
00:38:11,602 --> 00:38:12,478
‎You bet I did.

425
00:38:14,105 --> 00:38:15,731
‎Then do just one thing for me.

426
00:38:16,399 --> 00:38:19,944
‎Then you won't have to bother
‎swearing on your life

427
00:38:20,736 --> 00:38:22,613
‎for Cheon Yeo-ri
‎to lose my grandma's favor.

428
00:38:23,197 --> 00:38:25,699
‎It'll ruin her chances
‎of becoming a successor too.

429
00:38:26,826 --> 00:38:27,660
‎What do you say?

430
00:38:37,128 --> 00:38:38,254
‎Mr. Ma.

431
00:38:40,423 --> 00:38:42,550
‎What? I'm going to leave on time today.

432
00:38:42,633 --> 00:38:43,759
‎It's not that.

433
00:38:45,803 --> 00:38:46,720
‎It's Park Seung-jae.

434
00:38:48,264 --> 00:38:49,306
‎What about him?

435
00:38:51,809 --> 00:38:54,270
‎Park Seung-jae was granted
‎a motion for detention review?

436
00:38:54,353 --> 00:38:56,397
‎Why do you care?
‎It's not your case anymore.

437
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:58,107
‎It may not be my case, but still.

438
00:38:58,190 --> 00:39:00,443
‎It makes no sense that a murderer like him
‎is getting released!

439
00:39:00,526 --> 00:39:02,820
‎You think I granted it? The court did!

440
00:39:05,239 --> 00:39:06,073
‎SEOUL CENTRAL DISTRICT PROSECUTORS' OFFICE

441
00:39:06,157 --> 00:39:07,825
‎It was the prosecutor general's order.

442
00:39:08,742 --> 00:39:11,328
‎He has high hopes for the Cold Case Unit.

443
00:39:11,912 --> 00:39:14,165
‎Do a good job and score some points.

444
00:39:14,999 --> 00:39:17,835
‎And be gentle with the door
‎when you come and go.

445
00:39:19,044 --> 00:39:22,423
‎CORRECTIONAL SERVICES
‎ADVANCING ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

446
00:39:22,506 --> 00:39:23,549
‎-Well done.
‎-Good job.

447
00:39:23,632 --> 00:39:25,968
‎Man, I had the worst time in there.

448
00:39:26,051 --> 00:39:27,303
‎Hey, Park Seung-jae.

449
00:39:31,474 --> 00:39:32,433
‎What now?

450
00:39:33,017 --> 00:39:35,811
‎I was released by the law
‎that you love so much.

451
00:39:35,895 --> 00:39:37,521
‎I know your father got you out.

452
00:39:38,272 --> 00:39:39,607
‎It's my luck to have such a father.

453
00:39:39,690 --> 00:39:41,484
‎Yes, I know that too.

454
00:39:41,567 --> 00:39:45,196
‎I also know your father spent millions
‎to make you a golfer,

455
00:39:45,279 --> 00:39:48,365
‎and that you won the first trial
‎thanks to his connections.

456
00:39:48,449 --> 00:39:52,036
‎Man, getting screwed over like that
‎made me fixate on something.

457
00:39:52,661 --> 00:39:54,371
‎What might that be?

458
00:39:54,455 --> 00:39:56,874
‎I got some meaty intel

459
00:39:56,957 --> 00:39:59,502
‎about a reservoir
‎your father's slush fund is buried.

460
00:39:59,585 --> 00:40:00,586
‎Why you…

461
00:40:02,963 --> 00:40:04,006
‎Watch your back.

462
00:40:04,673 --> 00:40:07,676
‎You could get hurt
‎if you go after the wrong person.

463
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:09,094
‎You watch your own back.

464
00:40:09,178 --> 00:40:11,847
‎I have nothing to lose
‎because my job isn't my whole life.

465
00:40:12,765 --> 00:40:16,769
‎I guess I'd get no joy going after
‎a guy like you, just scraping by.

466
00:40:18,896 --> 00:40:22,858
‎I plan to find a weakness
‎instead of going after you.

467
00:40:23,734 --> 00:40:24,902
‎What are you on about?

468
00:40:25,486 --> 00:40:26,320
‎Cheon Yeo-ri.

469
00:40:29,573 --> 00:40:31,784
‎I just said her name.
‎What's with that look?

470
00:40:31,867 --> 00:40:34,328
‎Why would you bring her up right now?

471
00:40:34,411 --> 00:40:36,497
‎Wouldn't you love to know?

472
00:40:37,957 --> 00:40:38,916
‎Let's get going.

473
00:41:19,123 --> 00:41:21,250
‎CEO CHEON YEO-RI

474
00:41:22,501 --> 00:41:23,961
‎Even if we meet by chance,

475
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:26,088
‎let's pretend to be strangers.

476
00:41:33,178 --> 00:41:34,179
‎Yes, ma'am.

477
00:41:34,763 --> 00:41:36,807
‎I saw your message. Is something wrong?

478
00:41:36,890 --> 00:41:39,685
‎The Ministry of Foreign Affairs
‎called about the venue selection

479
00:41:39,768 --> 00:41:41,687
‎for the GA21 banquet.

480
00:41:41,770 --> 00:41:43,439
‎The inspection is in two days, right?

481
00:41:43,522 --> 00:41:46,609
‎They asked ‎if ‎it ‎could ‎be ‎moved up
‎to tomorrow instead.

482
00:41:47,318 --> 00:41:48,527
‎May I confirm with them?

483
00:41:49,528 --> 00:41:51,697
‎Go ahead. We're fully prepared anyway.

484
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:54,033
‎-Will do, ma'am.
‎-Bye.

485
00:42:02,833 --> 00:42:04,710
‎PROSECUTOR MA

486
00:43:25,374 --> 00:43:27,209
‎Who are you?

487
00:43:32,005 --> 00:43:34,675
‎Do I look like the Grim Reaper to you?

488
00:43:34,758 --> 00:43:37,428
‎Why are you digging a hole
‎in the middle of the night?

489
00:43:37,511 --> 00:43:39,221
‎I wanted to bury it right away.

490
00:43:39,930 --> 00:43:41,598
‎The clay jar with kimchi I just made.

491
00:43:41,682 --> 00:43:43,517
‎Why bury it outside
‎when I have a fridge for that?

492
00:43:44,017 --> 00:43:47,146
‎Besides, let your goons do the hard work.
‎They look like experts at that.

493
00:43:48,272 --> 00:43:49,690
‎Watch how you talk.

494
00:43:50,315 --> 00:43:51,984
‎I made this for you.

495
00:43:52,067 --> 00:43:54,069
‎I wouldn't let
‎anyone's grimy hands touch it.

496
00:43:55,487 --> 00:43:57,865
‎I'm worried you'll hurt your hips.

497
00:43:58,407 --> 00:43:59,867
‎Let's go inside.

498
00:44:00,451 --> 00:44:01,994
‎Are you worried I'll get hurt?

499
00:44:02,077 --> 00:44:03,912
‎Of course I'm worried.

500
00:44:05,038 --> 00:44:05,998
‎Here you go.

501
00:44:06,915 --> 00:44:10,002
‎No fridge can store food
‎as well as a clay jar.

502
00:44:10,085 --> 00:44:11,920
‎That's true. Plus, your touch works magic.

503
00:44:12,629 --> 00:44:13,630
‎Right?

504
00:44:15,591 --> 00:44:16,925
‎Try this too.

505
00:44:17,009 --> 00:44:19,470
‎-Here.
‎-Oh, thanks.

506
00:44:19,553 --> 00:44:22,306
‎You really weren't in Jeju Island?
‎I swear I saw you.

507
00:44:22,389 --> 00:44:24,808
‎Why do you keep asking
‎when I wasn't there?

508
00:44:25,809 --> 00:44:27,060
‎Remember how

509
00:44:27,144 --> 00:44:29,521
‎-you told me to beware of water?
‎-Yeah.

510
00:44:29,605 --> 00:44:32,357
‎The crazy thing is,
‎I fell into the sea that day.

511
00:44:35,235 --> 00:44:36,737
‎There's no need to be so shocked.

512
00:44:37,321 --> 00:44:39,364
‎I can swim as well as anyone.

513
00:44:39,448 --> 00:44:42,201
‎Don't you know that even
‎the best of people make mistakes?

514
00:44:42,785 --> 00:44:43,619
‎I do know that.

515
00:44:45,621 --> 00:44:47,873
‎So why did you fall into the water?

516
00:44:47,956 --> 00:44:48,957
‎Well…

517
00:44:51,460 --> 00:44:52,753
‎I slipped and lost my footing.

518
00:44:52,836 --> 00:44:54,004
‎I told you to be careful.

519
00:44:55,547 --> 00:44:57,090
‎-I will.
‎-Goodness…

520
00:44:58,133 --> 00:44:59,510
‎-Anyway,
‎-Oh, dear.

521
00:44:59,593 --> 00:45:02,471
‎the Year of the Black Monkey
‎you keep talking about.

522
00:45:02,554 --> 00:45:04,681
‎Did you hear that from a fortune-teller?

523
00:45:04,765 --> 00:45:05,599
‎Why?

524
00:45:06,308 --> 00:45:08,852
‎Are you seeing someone born in that year?

525
00:45:08,936 --> 00:45:11,271
‎Why would you say that?
‎I'm not seeing anyone.

526
00:45:12,314 --> 00:45:14,650
‎-I'm not.
‎-You're not, right?

527
00:45:15,651 --> 00:45:17,486
‎But what's the deal
‎with that specific year?

528
00:45:17,569 --> 00:45:19,947
‎There's nothing wrong
‎with the year itself.

529
00:45:20,030 --> 00:45:22,366
‎The problem is
‎that it's incompatible with you.

530
00:45:24,076 --> 00:45:24,910
‎Remember that.

531
00:45:24,993 --> 00:45:26,995
‎Okay, fine. Eat up.

532
00:45:30,457 --> 00:45:31,875
‎-One more thing.
‎-What?

533
00:45:31,959 --> 00:45:35,963
‎Don't go anywhere tonight.
‎Stay out of harm's way.

534
00:45:37,422 --> 00:45:38,257
‎Okay.

535
00:45:39,508 --> 00:45:42,386
‎You shouldn't cook so much.
‎You said your wrists hurt.

536
00:45:42,469 --> 00:45:45,055
‎-I'll order delivery. It's just as good.
‎-Enough.

537
00:45:45,138 --> 00:45:47,140
‎Delivery, my foot. Just eat.

538
00:46:01,822 --> 00:46:03,657
‎It must be my grandma's energy.

539
00:46:04,491 --> 00:46:06,076
‎I don't see any ghosts.

540
00:46:07,619 --> 00:46:08,996
‎Or is it because it's the last day?

541
00:46:13,959 --> 00:46:15,210
‎Oh, dear.

542
00:46:17,337 --> 00:46:19,506
‎I plan to find a weakness.

543
00:46:20,299 --> 00:46:21,133
‎Cheon Yeo-ri.

544
00:46:21,216 --> 00:46:23,218
‎Why would you bring her up right now?

545
00:46:23,302 --> 00:46:26,096
‎Wouldn't you love to know?

546
00:46:30,642 --> 00:46:32,269
‎CEO CHEON YEO-RI

547
00:46:34,313 --> 00:46:38,108
‎The phone is turned off.
‎You will be redirected to voicemail…

548
00:47:00,672 --> 00:47:01,590
‎Grandma?

549
00:47:03,216 --> 00:47:06,136
‎-That hurts.
‎-I told you not to go anywhere!

550
00:47:06,219 --> 00:47:07,804
‎Why won't you listen?

551
00:47:09,014 --> 00:47:10,223
‎Goodness.

552
00:47:11,350 --> 00:47:12,309
‎Stay right there.

553
00:47:13,018 --> 00:47:14,019
‎Jeez.

554
00:47:17,522 --> 00:47:19,024
‎She's so strong for her age.

555
00:47:20,025 --> 00:47:23,236
‎Does she know something
‎or is it just a hunch?

556
00:47:27,032 --> 00:47:30,243
‎Why did Cheon Yeo-ri
‎turn off her phone anyway?

557
00:47:41,171 --> 00:47:44,341
‎I feel nasty
‎because I only washed my hair earlier.

558
00:47:44,424 --> 00:47:47,636
‎I'll just take a shower
‎and go straight to bed, okay?

559
00:47:50,055 --> 00:47:51,640
‎Don't take too long.

560
00:47:54,559 --> 00:47:56,645
‎-Why you…
‎-Go to bed.

561
00:47:56,728 --> 00:47:58,397
‎Don't you dare go out.

562
00:47:58,480 --> 00:47:59,773
‎I won't.

563
00:48:15,664 --> 00:48:16,748
‎Hi.

564
00:48:19,835 --> 00:48:21,128
‎You're out of your mind.

565
00:48:21,878 --> 00:48:23,463
‎You're only adding to your charges.

566
00:48:23,547 --> 00:48:24,840
‎That's for me to take care of.

567
00:48:26,216 --> 00:48:27,509
‎I heard you ratted me out.

568
00:48:30,512 --> 00:48:31,471
‎Park Seung-jae.

569
00:48:33,140 --> 00:48:35,142
‎That's not called ratting out.

570
00:48:35,726 --> 00:48:36,977
‎It's called reporting a crime.

571
00:48:39,479 --> 00:48:41,648
‎Whatever you call it, you still did it.

572
00:48:45,610 --> 00:48:48,238
‎How did you know where Jang Eun-ju was?

573
00:48:49,990 --> 00:48:51,533
‎You really want to know that badly?

574
00:48:51,616 --> 00:48:52,784
‎Yes, I do.

575
00:48:52,868 --> 00:48:54,661
‎Ha-ri's right, isn't she?

576
00:48:55,495 --> 00:48:56,913
‎You see ghosts, don't you?

577
00:49:29,696 --> 00:49:31,323
‎F**D M*

578
00:49:35,786 --> 00:49:37,496
‎I heard Shaman Baek suppressed it,

579
00:49:38,997 --> 00:49:39,915
‎but it didn't work, did it?

580
00:49:39,998 --> 00:49:44,002
‎Whether I see ghosts or not,
‎how is that worth kidnapping me?

581
00:49:45,337 --> 00:49:46,838
‎It is worth kidnapping you.

582
00:49:47,881 --> 00:49:48,840
‎You see,

583
00:49:49,424 --> 00:49:50,300
‎it was Ha-ri's condition.

584
00:49:52,511 --> 00:49:54,513
‎She put you up to this?

585
00:49:54,596 --> 00:49:58,642
‎She said to bring back proof
‎that you can see ghosts.

586
00:50:00,227 --> 00:50:02,187
‎But that's not going to cut it.

587
00:50:02,854 --> 00:50:04,731
‎I need something more

588
00:50:04,815 --> 00:50:08,485
‎so you taste the monumental fall yourself.

589
00:50:09,236 --> 00:50:12,656
‎From what I heard,
‎there will be a big scandal out soon

590
00:50:12,739 --> 00:50:15,784
‎about a drug party with celebrities
‎and rich heirs and heiresses.

591
00:50:16,535 --> 00:50:18,662
‎I'm going to make sure
‎that your name is on the list.

592
00:50:18,745 --> 00:50:21,873
‎It'll be a little leverage
‎to keep you quiet.

593
00:50:22,916 --> 00:50:24,000
‎You crazy…

594
00:50:24,084 --> 00:50:25,168
‎Here.

595
00:50:38,098 --> 00:50:39,099
‎What's this punk doing?

596
00:51:16,177 --> 00:51:17,971
‎-Are you all right?
‎-Mr. Ma.

597
00:51:23,727 --> 00:51:24,644
‎Get up.

598
00:51:32,360 --> 00:51:33,361
‎Let's go.

599
00:51:34,321 --> 00:51:35,614
‎Get them, damn it!

600
00:51:37,324 --> 00:51:39,910
‎-How did you find me?
‎-Let's get out of here first.

601
00:51:39,993 --> 00:51:40,827
‎Damn it!

602
00:52:38,259 --> 00:52:39,094
‎Shit!

603
00:52:40,720 --> 00:52:41,846
‎Mr. Ma!

604
00:52:44,933 --> 00:52:47,018
‎-Gang-uk.
‎-Mr. Ma.

605
00:52:47,102 --> 00:52:48,436
‎-Oh, no.
‎-Mr. Ma!

606
00:52:48,979 --> 00:52:49,854
‎Are you okay?

607
00:52:49,938 --> 00:52:52,524
‎-Call for help!
‎-Quick, call an ambulance!

608
00:52:52,607 --> 00:52:54,985
‎-Are you all right?
‎-Don't touch him.

609
00:53:01,783 --> 00:53:02,909
‎Careful.

610
00:53:04,327 --> 00:53:06,371
‎-The ambulance!
‎-Did you call for one?

611
00:53:06,454 --> 00:53:07,372
‎Tell them to hurry!

612
00:53:08,957 --> 00:53:11,126
‎-Wake up! There's blood…
‎-Don't move him.

613
00:53:12,335 --> 00:53:14,546
‎Mr. Ma, wake up.

614
00:53:18,383 --> 00:53:19,217
‎Mr. Ma.

615
00:53:20,844 --> 00:53:21,720
‎Mr. Ma!

616
00:53:24,055 --> 00:53:24,889
‎Mr. Ma.

617
00:53:53,043 --> 00:53:57,047
‎He's a traffic accident victim.
‎Found unconscious, BP is 80 over 40.

618
00:53:57,130 --> 00:53:59,299
‎O2 saturation went down to 89,
‎so we put him on oxygen.

619
00:53:59,382 --> 00:54:00,967
‎Mr. Ma! Hurry!

620
00:54:01,051 --> 00:54:01,926
‎Mr. Ma!

621
00:54:04,596 --> 00:54:05,597
‎Please, Mr. Ma.

622
00:54:08,349 --> 00:54:09,184
‎Mr. Ma!

623
00:54:23,364 --> 00:54:24,532
‎-Mr. Ma.
‎-Wait outside.

624
00:54:24,616 --> 00:54:27,243
‎-You can't come in! Stay here!
‎-Mr. Ma!

625
00:54:27,327 --> 00:54:28,828
‎-Okay.
‎-Sir?

626
00:54:28,912 --> 00:54:30,580
‎Do you hear me?

627
00:54:30,663 --> 00:54:32,707
‎Sir. What's your name?

628
00:54:34,417 --> 00:54:36,044
‎-Check for a pulse.
‎-Okay.

629
00:54:38,129 --> 00:54:40,465
‎He's in Ventricular tachycardia.
‎Starting CPR.

630
00:54:40,548 --> 00:54:42,175
‎-Get a defibrillator.
‎-Okay.

631
00:54:43,885 --> 00:54:46,763
‎-What's wrong? Why are they doing that?
‎-Damn it.

632
00:54:46,846 --> 00:54:48,848
‎-What are they doing?
‎-You can't come in.

633
00:54:48,932 --> 00:54:51,893
‎Take good care of him! Please save him!

634
00:54:51,976 --> 00:54:53,061
‎Mr. Ma!

635
00:55:01,986 --> 00:55:02,946
‎Let's change places.

636
00:55:17,919 --> 00:55:19,504
‎Gang-uk!

637
00:55:20,088 --> 00:55:21,089
‎Gang-uk…

638
00:55:26,386 --> 00:55:27,387
‎Gang-uk!

639
00:55:29,722 --> 00:55:30,974
‎Gang-uk…

640
00:55:31,057 --> 00:55:32,142
‎Mr. Ma!

641
00:55:33,101 --> 00:55:34,102
‎Mr. Ma!

642
00:56:27,113 --> 00:56:28,364
‎It's my fault.

643
00:56:31,034 --> 00:56:32,202
‎Because of me…

644
00:56:43,504 --> 00:56:45,298
‎I could barely get through a week.

645
00:56:46,466 --> 00:56:49,427
‎How did you manage to endure it
‎for ten whole years?

646
00:56:52,222 --> 00:56:53,765
‎I'll try to get through it on my own.

647
00:56:54,766 --> 00:56:56,267
‎I'm an adult, after all.

648
00:56:56,351 --> 00:56:58,019
‎Much more so than you were back then.

649
00:57:06,027 --> 00:57:07,028
‎Here.

650
00:57:09,781 --> 00:57:12,825
‎Let's stay away from each other
‎as best we can.

651
00:57:13,326 --> 00:57:16,246
‎If you're around me,
‎you might become miserable.

652
00:57:20,959 --> 00:57:21,876
‎Mr. Ma.

653
00:57:22,752 --> 00:57:26,256
‎I suspected you as an accomplice,
‎not knowing about your background.

654
00:57:26,756 --> 00:57:27,924
‎I'm sorry.

655
00:57:29,300 --> 00:57:31,386
‎It must've been so hard to live with.

656
00:58:27,400 --> 00:58:28,359
‎Mr. Ma?

657
00:58:33,865 --> 00:58:35,033
‎Gang-uk.

658
00:58:37,785 --> 00:58:38,911
‎Oh, no…

659
00:58:41,623 --> 00:58:42,915
‎Because of me,

660
00:58:44,626 --> 00:58:47,170
‎you turned into a ghost already
‎and came to see me?

661
00:58:50,048 --> 00:58:51,174
‎Oh, no…

662
00:58:54,594 --> 00:58:56,137
‎Oh, gosh…

663
01:00:06,874 --> 01:00:09,252
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

664
01:00:09,335 --> 01:00:11,587
‎Reporters are already
‎swarming ‎outside Reina.

665
01:00:12,380 --> 01:00:14,507
‎Should there be any
‎speculative articles or photos,

666
01:00:14,590 --> 01:00:18,052
‎we will take strong legal action,
‎so please step back.

667
01:00:18,136 --> 01:00:19,512
‎They're birds of a feather.

668
01:00:19,595 --> 01:00:22,056
‎Are you doing this ‎because
‎you ‎really want to marry Min-hwan?

669
01:00:22,140 --> 01:00:22,974
‎Cheon Ha-ri.

670
01:00:23,057 --> 01:00:26,269
‎Director Ok,
‎should we acquire another masterpiece?

671
01:00:26,352 --> 01:00:29,981
‎Yeeon Museum of Art.
‎The director there is pretty influential.

672
01:00:30,064 --> 01:00:31,858
‎Reina Hotel's slush fund allegations?

673
01:00:31,941 --> 01:00:35,695
‎The artworks displayed at the hotel
‎are supplied by Gallery Cheon, right?

674
01:00:35,778 --> 01:00:37,655
‎How much do you know ‎about ‎Yeo-ri?

675
01:00:37,739 --> 01:00:39,198
‎Don't you want to know?

676
01:00:39,282 --> 01:00:40,992
‎Some rumors started
‎after the engagement fell through.

677
01:00:41,075 --> 01:00:41,993
‎Who's there?

678
01:00:42,076 --> 01:00:44,370
‎A bastard like him
‎doesn't deserve to be human.

679
01:00:45,371 --> 01:00:47,749
‎Who are you? Who the hell are you?

680
01:00:47,832 --> 01:00:49,792
‎-Let go.
‎-Damn it.

681
01:00:49,876 --> 01:00:52,628
‎I'll make you regret this.

682
01:00:52,712 --> 01:00:56,674
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim

